                <pb facs="0865" n="747" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg747"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.7112A/6: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Rumania</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Patterson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-08-10T16:00:00-04:00">August 10, 1928—4
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>30. Rumanian Minister has stated his Government glad to negotiate treaty of
                    arbitration and treaty of conciliation with United States and expressed hope
                    treaties may be signed before my departure on August seventeenth. To enable this
                    necessary Minister should have full powers. Say to Minister for Foreign Affairs
                    that if autographed full powers mentioning both treaties or separate full powers
                    in each case be exhibited to you, you will be glad to cable their texts in full
                    to me. Cable promptly.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
